{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Some time later Joash resolved
To re[Abmaj7]store the house of the [Eb]LORD
He [Abmaj7]gathered priests and [Eb]Levites
To col[Abmaj7]lect money from all [Bb]Israel
[Eb]But they did not act quickly
The [Abmaj7]chief priest asked for the [Cm]tax
[Abmaj7]Laid down by Mo[Eb/G]ses in the wilderness
[Abmaj7]For the tent of the testimo[Eb]ny
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
They [Ab]made a chest at [Eb]the gate
And the peo[Bb]ple dropped their [Cm]silver in
All [Ab]the officials [Eb]rejoiced
And the [Bb]chest was filled [Cm]to the [Ab]brim
Stonecutters and car[Eb/G]penters worked
To restore [Bb]the origi[Cm]nal de[Ab]sign
The workmen la[Eb/G]bored day by day
[Ab]And the house [Bb]of God was [Eb]made whole
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
