{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
At[Eb]haliah had broken in
And used [Ab]sacred things for [Eb]Baal
Now the [Ab]king commanded repair
[Eb/G]And the work went [Bb]forward
The [Eb]Levites carried the chest
To [Ab]the king’s offi[Cm7]cers each day
A [Ab]large amount of mon[Eb/G]ey
Was col[Ab]lected for the tem[Eb]ple
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
They made a [Ab]chest at the gate
[Eb]And the people dropped [Bb]their silver [Cm]in
All the of[Ab]ficials rejoiced
[Eb]And the chest was [Bb]filled to the [Cm]brim
Stone[Ab]cutters and carpenters [Eb/G]worked
To restore the o[Bb]riginal de[Cm]sign
The [Ab]workmen labored day [Eb/G]by day
And the [Ab]house of [Bb]God was made [Eb]whole
{end_of_chorus}

